478	Its ledger is `RUN_RESULT_VERSIONS.json`, entries `{ "schema_version", "schemaSha256", "note" }`, newest last, under the same rule: the newest entry carries the SHA-256 of the checked-in schema and the current `RUN_RESULT_SCHEMA_VERSION`. An added optional member keeps the version; a removed or renamed member, or a changed type or meaning, bumps it. The schema covers every type the result reaches (`TurnResult`, `ValidationReceipt` and the rest), so a change to any of them needs a regenerated schema and an entry. `cli/test/run_json_contract.test.ts` runs the comparison. The manual (`docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, "`nexus run --json`") describes the document and the exit codes.
479	
480	## The `nexus verify --json` document
481	
482	`verify-result-v1.schema.json` is the JSON Schema of the one document `nexus verify --json` prints and `--receipt <file>` writes (`VerifyJsonOutput` in `cli/src/verify_contract.ts`: a result with `verdict`, or an error document without one). It is generated by the same `SchemaBuilder`; the two command-result generators share `cli/scripts/result_schema.mjs`.
483	
484	```bash
485	cd cli
486	node scripts/gen_verify_result_schema.mjs           # rewrite docs/protocol/verify-result-v1.schema.json
487	node scripts/gen_verify_result_schema.mjs --check   # exit 1 when the schema or its ledger is stale
488	```
489	
490	Its ledger is `VERIFY_RESULT_VERSIONS.json`, entries `{ "schema_version", "schemaSha256", "note" }`, newest last, under the same rule as the run-result ledger with `VERIFY_RESULT_SCHEMA_VERSION`. The schema reaches `VerificationEvidence` and `TypecheckEvidence` (`cli/src/core/turn.ts`) and the guard's classes and modes (`cli/src/security.ts`), so a change to any of them needs a regenerated schema and an entry here as well as for the run result. `cli/test/verify_schema.test.ts` runs the comparison, and every result document the `nexus verify` tests produce is validated against the schema. The manual (`docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, "`nexus verify`") describes the document and the exit codes.
491	
492	## The audit bundle
493	
494	`audit-bundle-v1.schema.json` is the JSON Schema of the two documents an audit bundle carries (`AuditBundleDocument` in `cli/src/audit_contract.ts`): `manifest.json` (`AuditManifest`) and the detached signature envelope `manifest.sig.json` (`AuditSignatureEnvelope`). `audit-verify-result-v1.schema.json` is the schema of the one document a verification of a bundle prints (`AuditVerifyOutput`: a result with `result`, or an error document without one). Both are generated by the same `SchemaBuilder` through `cli/scripts/result_schema.mjs`.
495	
496	```bash
497	cd cli
498	node scripts/gen_audit_schema.mjs           # rewrite both schemas
499	node scripts/gen_audit_schema.mjs --check   # exit 1 when a schema or its ledger is stale
500	```
501	
502	Their ledgers are `AUDIT_BUNDLE_VERSIONS.json` and `AUDIT_VERIFY_RESULT_VERSIONS.json`, entries `{ "schema_version", "schemaSha256", "note" }`, newest last, under the same rule as the run-result ledger with `AUDIT_BUNDLE_SCHEMA_VERSION` and `AUDIT_VERIFY_RESULT_SCHEMA_VERSION`. The bundle schema reaches `ChainLink` (`cli/src/core/hash_chain.ts`), so a change there needs a regenerated schema and an entry. `cli/test/audit_schema.test.ts` runs the comparison and pins the exit-code table (`AUDIT_EXIT_CODES`); every manifest written and every result produced in `cli/test/audit_bundle.test.ts` is validated against the schemas.
503	
504	A schema describes a document's shape only. What makes a bundle verify is defined in `cli/src/core/audit_bundle.ts`: `manifest.json` is exactly the canonical JSON of the manifest (keys sorted at every depth, no whitespace) and one newline; a file's `sha256` is over its bytes; each entry of `files` is linked to the one before it with `linkRecord`; `root_sha256` is the SHA-256 of the canonical JSON of the manifest without that member. An unsigned bundle that verifies is self-consistent, which does not show who wrote it: anyone able to write the bundle can replace its files and the manifest together. The envelope is declared here so the schema is stable; nothing writes or checks a signature yet.
